      "id": "claim_38942685db3d44a3bae607489d3dd0f8",
      "statement": "`packages/ui` declares `react` and `react-dom` `^18.2.0` as regular runtime dependencies while its devDependencies type them with `@types/react` `^19.0.1` and `@types/react-dom` `^19.0.2`, so the declared types are a major version ahead of the declared runtime and React is declared as a regular dependency rather than a peer dependency — meaning a consuming app would install a nested React copy instead of sharing its own.",
